# This repository contains byte-exact text goldens that tests compare as whole
# strings: rendered hex dumps, a generated Swift enum, a cross-binding parity
# JSON fixture. On a Windows clone git's default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites
# every LF to CRLF on checkout, after which those comparisons fail for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the engine. Normalising the working tree to LF on
# every platform is the only setting under which a Windows checkout and the
# macOS/Linux checkouts hold the same bytes.
#
# The persisted binary formats are unaffected either way -- these are text
# renderings of golden bytes, not the bytes themselves.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact fixtures additionally opt out of normalisation entirely, so
# nothing can be rewritten on the way into the index either.
crates/zeppelin-embed/tests/fixtures/** -text
bindings/fixtures/** -text

# Shell scripts must stay LF so they remain executable when a Windows checkout
# is used from WSL, Git Bash or a container.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets are never line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.svg -text
*.node binary
